{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For she was afraid, etc.; for you did laugh.</b> The first serves as דְּהָא — giving the reason for the matter: Sarah denied it because she was afraid. The second serves as אֶלָּא — 'He said, No, it is not as you say, אֶלָּא you did laugh.' As our Rabbis said: כִּי serves in four senses: אִי, דִּלְמָא, אֶלָּא, דְּהָא."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:15.018325030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}